@startuml
' sys_identity — rewritten by 01_system so it renders, keeping what it means.
'
' WHY THE PREVIOUS SOURCE FAILED, most likely cause first:
'   1. "$external database user" — PlantUML's preprocessor reads $name as a
'      variable reference. An undefined variable in a label is the classic
'      silent parse failure, and this file had one in an element NAME.
'      Written here as &#36;external, which renders as the dollar sign.
'   2. class bodies mixed with component/artifact/database elements in one
'      diagram. Every element here is a rectangle, which every renderer
'      accepts, and the member lists are label text rather than class members.
'   3. Stereotypes carrying a colon, e.g. <<Atlas, kind: certificate>>.
'      Folded into the label text instead.
' LEGIBILITY (measured 2263x1093 = 362 px/in as placed, unreadable in print):
' the seven identities and the four packages each laid out side by side. Chained
' vertically with hidden arrows so the layout runs down the page; a tall diagram
' gets the full height of a portrait page. No element or relationship removed.
'
' Notes and package blocks are kept — the coordinator established neither is
' the cause, and both carry meaning here.
'
' CONTENT IS ALSO CORRECTED. The previous source stated the agent's role as
' the constrained one. That is what the repository declares; it is not what
' the platform holds. The divergence is the most important fact in this
' picture and is now drawn rather than omitted.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam nodesep 8
skinparam ranksep 14

title Who ChatHealthy.ai can act as, where each credential is kept, and what proves it

package "The directory — every identity in the tenant" #eef2ff {

  rectangle "**the operator**\n//person//\n----\nOwner\nUser Access Administrator\nGlobal Administrator" as SKIP #fff7ed

  rectangle "**claudeCodeAgent**\n//agent — service principal//\n----\nDECLARED in the repository:\nchatHealthyAgent, with identity creation\nand role-definition writes withheld,\nplus a condition it cannot remove\n----\nHELD on the platform:\nthe same role withholding nothing,\nplus unconditioned Owner and\nUser Access Administrator above it" as CCA #fee2e2

  rectangle "**DevOpsUser**\n//agent — service principal//\n----\nvault administration\nautomation, container and site contributor\nregistry push, blob write, monitoring read\ndirectory read\nrole_governance_recorder" as DEVOPS

  rectangle "**pipelineEditor**\n//agent — service principal//\n----\nvault secrets read\nautomation operator, registry pull\nmachine and network contributor\nblob write, reader" as PEDIT

  rectangle "**frontendUser**\n//agent — service principal//\n----\nvault secrets read, and nothing else" as FEUSER

  rectangle "**dataMigrator**\n//agent — managed identity//\n----\nvault secrets read\nrole_data_migrator" as MIG

  rectangle "**ClaudeCodeUser**\n//user object//\n----\nholds no rights and signs in nowhere" as CCU

  ' Stack the identities so this package runs down the page, not across it.
  SKIP -[hidden]down- CCA
  CCA -[hidden]down- DEVOPS
  DEVOPS -[hidden]down- PEDIT
  PEDIT -[hidden]down- FEUSER
  FEUSER -[hidden]down- MIG
  MIG -[hidden]down- CCU
}

package "The certificate authority" #fefce8 {
  rectangle "**ChatHealthy CA**\nroot and intermediate\n----\nthe chain is baked into images at build time\n----\n**the minting path is absent from disk;**\n**the caller that issues still imports it**" as CA #fee2e2
}

package "Custody — the credential vault" #f0fdfa {
  rectangle "**one certificate-and-key per identity**\nthe secret is named for the identity it belongs to" as IDCERTS
  rectangle "**store control-plane API keys**\na read-only pair and a lifecycle pair,\ndeliberately separate" as ATLASKEYS
  rectangle "**third-party API keys**\nmodel vendors, maps, mail,\nthe edge header, the source URLs" as OTHERSECRETS
  IDCERTS -[hidden]down- ATLASKEYS
  ATLASKEYS -[hidden]down- OTHERSECRETS
}

package "The data platform" #ecfdf5 {

  rectangle "**serving store**" as ATF
  rectangle "**pipeline store**" as ATP

  rectangle "**certificate-authenticated database user**\n//the username is the certificate subject//\n----\nthe subject common name must equal\nthe identity being asked for\n----\nregistered against the &#36;external database" as DBUSER

  rectangle "**role_data_migrator**\n//custom database role//\n----\nread on the built data\ninsert and create on the served data\nread and **insert** on the approvals\ndelete on its own job lock only\n----\nno update, no delete, no drop over data" as RDM

  rectangle "**role_governance_recorder**\n//custom database role//\n----\nread and insert on the governance store\n----\nno update, no delete, no drop\nand the recorder is not the actor" as RGR

  rectangle "**certificate registry**\nidentity, subject, vault key names,\ncreated, expires, status, version\n----\n**required, and nothing reads or writes it**" as REG #fee2e2

  ATF -- REG
  ATF -[hidden]down- ATP
  ATP -[hidden]down- DBUSER
  DBUSER -[hidden]down- RDM
  RDM -[hidden]down- RGR
}

' Chain the packages so the whole diagram runs down the page.
CCU -[hidden]down- CA
OTHERSECRETS -[hidden]down- ATF

CA --> IDCERTS : issues a certificate for a subject\nand stores it under the identity's name
IDCERTS --> REG : the registry says which secret\nholds which identity's certificate

CCA ..> IDCERTS
DEVOPS ..> IDCERTS
PEDIT ..> IDCERTS
FEUSER ..> IDCERTS
MIG ..> IDCERTS

IDCERTS --> DBUSER : the certificate is presented\nover mutual TLS
DBUSER --> ATF
DBUSER --> ATP
RDM --> DBUSER
RGR --> DBUSER
MIG ..> RDM
DEVOPS ..> RGR

ATLASKEYS --> RDM : **the control plane that defines these roles**\n**is reachable from a key on the workstation**

note bottom of SKIP
  The only person, and the only identity in the
  tenant that may bring another identity into
  existence. That is the one capability an agent
  is never granted.
end note

note bottom of CCA
  The gap between DECLARED and HELD is the finding.
  A permission list is not a boundary: the withheld
  capability is reachable by a second, unconditioned
  assignment at a higher scope, so the condition is
  applied and governs nothing.
end note

note bottom of CCU
  It exists only because the directory will not accept
  a service principal as a group's last owner, so the
  agent groups need a user object to own them.
end note

note bottom of DBUSER
  The subject is checked against the identity being
  requested before the connection opens. Without that,
  a mis-stored secret authenticates as whoever its
  certificate names and no caller can tell.
end note

note bottom of RDM
  Insert on the approvals is needed so the service can
  record its acknowledgement — but a store grant is per
  collection, not per document kind, so the identity that
  performs the release can write the record that releases
  it. Append-only stops alteration, not origination.
end note

@enduml
